{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "This was an UPFRONT_QUOTE trip. The fare breakdown records fare_model = UPFRONT_QUOTE with a quoted_fare_sgd of 34.50 fixed at booking, so the distance and time lines were closed at that moment. Under POL-RD-11 the platform does not recompute them: POL-RD-02 does not run and 'no distance-or-time refund is available to the rider however large the excess'. The rider's demand to refund 'the extra distance' therefore fails on the fare model itself, quite apart from the mileage, and the driver's unrecovered cost on the detour is expressly not recoverable from the rider under this clause.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.fare_model",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The SGD 2.50 KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) line is a legitimate pass-through and is not refundable. It is marked on_optimal_route = true, and the 10-second trace passes within 44.5 m of that gantry (fix 136), well inside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09 lays down for treating a fix as a crossing. ERP actually crossed on the optimal route is properly chargeable and is not returned to the rider.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[0].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's entitlement under POL-RD-11 is capped at the amount by which the charged total of SGD 39.00 exceeds the SGD 34.50 quote plus the pass-through lines properly chargeable under POL-RD-09. The only properly chargeable pass-through is the SGD 2.50 KPE gantry, so the ceiling is SGD 39.00 less (SGD 34.50 + SGD 2.50) = SGD 2.00. The remaining SGD 4.00 of the SGD 6.00 contested has no basis in the record and the present state as to it should stand.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-00115", "EV-GPS-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-11", "POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.erp_lines",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "I concede the one point that is genuinely on the rider's side. The SGD 2.00 AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line is not matched by the trace: the closest the vehicle ever comes to that gantry is 5,419 m, far outside the 250 m match radius. That is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4) and is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. The driver does not oppose that SGD 2.00; he never went near the AYE and says so; and it is not a finding against him. It is also the whole of the rider's entitlement.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-FARE-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-09"],
      "relies_on": "derived.erp_gantry_proximity.lines[1].nearest_fix.distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The trace does show an excess — 5.78 km, 25.8% against the 22.4 km optimal, measured on the GPS polyline that POL-RD-01 makes the governing figure — so a deviation is established. It is not, however, MATERIAL: 25.8% is below the 50% limb and 5.78 km is below the 8.0 km limb. POL-RD-06 is therefore not engaged, the driver_profile check does not run, and no driver-conduct referral follows from this trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-00115", "EV-TRIP-00115"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-01", "POL-RD-06"],
      "relies_on": "derived.deviation.excess_pct",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver's own explanation — heavy CTE traffic — is not carried by the record and I do not press it. The LTA advisory artifact for the 21:06-21:48 window is MISSING under issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT at weight 0.0, so no traffic_advisory names the CTE or any corridor the optimal route uses, and POL-RD-03 exoneration fails for want of the required artifact. POL-RD-08 is equally clear that a bare assertion of bad traffic, unsupported by an advisory ID, discharges nothing. The point is moot for the money, because POL-RD-11 caps the rider's recovery at SGD 2.00 in any event.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-00115-01"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-RD-03", "POL-RD-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing integrity: the SGD 2.00 AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) gantry line on the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00115) was never crossed by the vehicle — the closest GPS fix is 5,419 m away, far outside the 250 m match radius — and is refunded in full as a standalone correction."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "This was an upfront-quoted trip: the fare breakdown (EV-FARE-00115) records fare_model = UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd = 34.50. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges were fixed at booking, so POL-RD-02 does not run and no distance-or-time refund is available however large the excess. The GPS trace does establish a route deviation — 28.18 km driven against a 22.4 km optimal, an excess of 5.78 km (25.8%) — but on an upfront fare that deviation costs the rider nothing on the distance lines, so the request to 'refund the extra distance' fails on the fare model itself. The deviation is established but not MATERIAL (25.8% is below the 50% limb and 5.78 km is below the 8.0 km limb), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check is not engaged; in any event the driver's trailing figures (deviation_flags_90d = 1 against completed_trips_90d = 174, far below the 0.05 ratio) show no pattern, and no driver-conduct referral follows.\n\nThe refund is the overcharge on the total. You were charged SGD 39.00 against the SGD 34.50 quote, and the SGD 4.50 difference is entirely ERP. The KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) line of SGD 2.50 is properly chargeable: the trace passes within 44.5 m of that gantry and it lies on the optimal route, so it is not returned. The AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) line of SGD 2.00 is different: the trace never comes closer than 5,419 m, so the vehicle never crossed that gantry. That is a billing-integrity failure under POL-RD-09(4), refunded in full as a standalone correction available whether or not a deviation exists, and recorded in the referrals above. Because it is the only unmatched charge line and it is refunded under POL-RD-09(4), POL-RD-10(8) does not escalate the case.\n\nArithmetic: charged_total 39.00 less (quoted_fare 34.50 + ERP actually crossed 2.50) = SGD 2.00, refunded in full under POL-RD-11(a). That SGD 2.00 is also exactly the phantom AYE line, so nothing is counted twice.\n\nOn the driver's attempted exoneration: POL-RD-04 is unavailable. The only message naming a route ('CTE very heavy boss, i go KPE then TPE') was sent by the driver, not the rider, and the rider's reply 'ok' names no place or road; with waypoint_hint null on both messages the corroboration test cannot be run, so the clause is unavailable and POL-RD-09(3) does not bar the ERP correction. The driver's heavy-traffic explanation is not carried by any artifact: the LTA advisory for the window is missing — EV-ADVIS-00115-01, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — so POL-RD-03 has no advisory to run on, and a bare assertion of bad traffic discharges nothing under POL-RD-08.\n\nThe trace itself is clean under POL-RD-07 (229 fixes at a steady 10 s interval, 100% coverage, no gaps, max gap 0 s), so it is not impaired for policy purposes and needs no independent corroboration or POL-RD-10(3) escalation; its schema-level status is COMPLETE and it is used at full weight.\n\nOn the profiles: no profile field is used as a ground of decision. Only deviation_flags_90d and completed_trips_90d are citable under POL-RD-06 and they show no pattern; the remaining fields (including prior_deviation_flags, rating, account_age_days, lifetime_trips) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and were not relied on.\n\nReading NO_ACTION party-relatively is correct, but no NO_ACTION is reached here: this is a rider-filed dispute with payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.0, so the SGD 2.00 is a real refund to the rider. Confidence rests on facts carried by EV-FARE-00115 and EV-GPS-00115, both at full weight 1.0; neither is impaired, so the cap is 1.0."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding: the SGD 2.00 'AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas)' ERP line is billed on a trip whose GPS trace never comes within 250 m of that gantry (closest approach 5,419.29 m, at fix index 0); the line is refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction and is referred for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To both parties. Distance. This booking was an UPFRONT_QUOTE at SGD 34.50, so POL-RD-11 governs and POL-RD-02 does not run. The GPS trace does show a real route deviation: 28.18 km driven against the 22.4 km booking optimal, an excess of 5.78 km (25.80%), which passes both POL-RD-01 establishment tests. It is not, however, a MATERIAL deviation (25.80% is below 50% and 5.78 km is below 8.0 km), so the POL-RD-06 driver-profile check does not run and no driver-conduct referral follows. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time lines were fixed at booking, so no part of the excess distance is refundable to the rider however large it is, and the driver cannot recover it from the rider either. That part of the claim is not payable. The charge. charged_total was SGD 39.00 against the SGD 34.50 quote, a gap of SGD 4.50, made up of two ERP lines: KPE (Defu Flyover towards ECP) SGD 2.50 and AYE (Alexandra Rd towards Tuas) SGD 2.00. The KPE gantry lies on the optimal route and the trace passes within 44.5 m of it, so it was genuinely crossed and is properly chargeable. The AYE line is different: the trace never comes closer than 5,419 m to that gantry, far outside the 250 m match radius POL-RD-09 lays down; driver, you say you never went near the AYE, and the telemetry agrees. That SGD 2.00 is a phantom charge. So SGD 39.00 less (the SGD 34.50 quote plus the SGD 2.50 gantry actually crossed) = SGD 2.00, refunded in full under POL-RD-11(a) and refunded separately and in full as a standalone correction under POL-RD-09(4); these are the same SGD 2.00 and are not counted twice. The refund is SGD 2.00 of the SGD 6.00 contested. Traffic. Driver, your explanation that the CTE was heavy cites no LTA advisory ID and no evidence ID; under POL-RD-08 that bare assertion carries no weight and discharges nothing, and POL-RD-03 exoneration cannot run without an advisory. There is no advisory on file: EV-ADVIS-00115-01 is MISSING (weight 0.0, issue MISSING_ARTIFACT), which is why nothing is exonerated on that ground; the absence itself is not held against you. Rider, I accept your reading that the two-message chat ('CTE very heavy boss, i go KPE then TPE' from the driver, 'ok' from you) does not amount to a rider instruction under POL-RD-04, so POL-RD-09(3) does not bar the ERP correction; that point is moot for the money in any event. No escalation. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07 (229 fixes, steady 10-second interval, no gaps, 100% coverage); the trip identifiers match across trip record, trace and fare breakdown; and the only charge line with no counterpart in the trace is the AYE line, which is refunded under POL-RD-09(4) and so does not engage POL-RD-10(8). The driver's heavy-traffic remark is a bare assertion under POL-RD-08 rather than an exculpatory clause invoked against a cited artifact, so POL-RD-10(5) does not fire. No POL-RD-10 trigger applies and no escalation issues. Referral. The unmatched AYE line is recorded as a POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity finding for platform review. Confidence. Every deciding figure (quote, charged total, gantry lines, deviation) is carried by full-weight artifacts — EV-FARE-00115, EV-GPS-00115 and EV-TRIP-00115, all at weight 1.0 — so confidence is high."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
